B65 BASIC v0.3 (45GS02) for MEGA65
Derived from BBC BASIC (Z80) v5
(C) Copyright R.T.Russell 2025
MEGA65 (model $03), 384K chip RAM, 8MB attic RAM

>1 REM Core: K325T feature level 3 (step 6) for the 64 list-mode balls; any other MEGA65 core: 8 sprite balls. Not on K325T levels 1-2.
>5 REM Per frame (64 balls), Xemu, no vsync wait: about 14 ms (move loop about 13.3, 210 us a ball; star planes 0.6: 8 writes, one 8-job DMA) + about 1.3 ms a colliding pair: 50 fps. RRB row: 6x4x(GOTOX+star) = 48 tokens (no XCTL bit 3: +GOTOX+80 black)
>10 REM Bounce: N% balls that bounce off the walls and off each other (B65),
>12 REM in front of four parallax star planes (1/4, 1/2, 1, 2 pixels a frame)
>20 REM K325T core: the balls are RRB list mode v2 objects (shaded full-colour
>30 REM glyphs from an own 256-colour palette, 640x400) and the core's
>40 REM collision engine compares all of them once per frame: ON COLLISION
>50 REM PROChit then runs between statements and COLLIDE(i) gives ball i's
>60 REM first partner. The engine tests boxes, inclusive edges (here 6x8:
>70 REM table +14 = 6 for an 8-pixel ball), so it fires a little early at the
>80 REM diagonals: every pair is confirmed with the centre distance
>85 REM (dx*dx+dy*dy <= 64, two radius-4 balls) before the two velocities are
>90 REM swapped and both balls moved one step apart (no new collision then).
>95 REM Position and velocity of a ball are one integer each (X + 65536*Y), so
>96 REM one addition moves a ball and the same value (AND &3FF03FF: v2 X/Y AND
>97 REM 1023) goes into the object table.
>100 REM Elsewhere (Xemu, standard MEGA65): the first 8 balls are sprites, the
>105 REM pairs are found in BASIC only with SW%=1 (tests; slow with many balls).
>110 REM BN%>0: stop after BN% frames (tests); RS%=1: back to text, timing;
>115 REM G%=1: gravity. BASIC 65 twin: examples/basic65/bounce65.bas (32 balls).
>120 BN%=0:RS%=1:N%=64:G%=0:SW%=0:BW%=6
>130 TB%=&8C000:GA%=&60000:OA%=&89000:OC%=&7800:S%=&80000:CR%=&FF84000:ZL%=&90000:ZH%=&A8000:ZS%=&BC000:SG%=6:K%=(?&6E1=&FF)
>135 IF K%=0 THEN S%=&50000:GA%=&58000:ZL%=&8400000:ZH%=&8420000:ZS%=&54000:REM (no chip RAM at &60000-&FFFFF: attic)
>140 DIM P%(N%),V%(N%),LB% 255,DT% 543,ZD%(3),ZA%(3),ZK%(7):PROCtables
>150 V1%=?&D031:V5%=?&D05B:V7%=?&D07B:ON ERROR PROCtext:REPORT:PRINT " at line ";ERL:END
>160 PROCpalsave:CLS:PRINT "Bounce: ";N%;" balls":PROCpalette:PROCballs
>170 REM start on a grid (no overlaps), random velocities -3..3 (not 0)
>175 GC%=16:GX%=39:GY%=90:IF N%>64 THEN GC%=24:GX%=26:GY%=36:REM (up to 264 balls)
>180 Q=RND(-42):FOR I%=0 TO N%-1:P%(I%)=12+(I% MOD GC%)*GX%+(20+(I% DIV GC%)*GY%)*65536
>190 REPEAT U%=RND(7)-4:UNTIL U%:REPEAT W%=RND(7)-4:UNTIL W%:V%(I%)=U%+W%*65536:NEXT
>200 PROCscreen:IF K% THEN ON COLLISION PROChit ELSE PROCsprites
>210 REM main loop: wait for the frame, let PROChit run (EI), then move every
>220 REM ball without events (DI; walls: PROCwall, a negative X or Y shows as
>225 REM a large one) and write X/Y with HOLD around the batch (all move at
>226 REM once); without the K325T the table and HOLD go to scratch RAM
>230 F%=0:NP%=0:T%=TIME:IF K%=0 THEN TB%=&5D000:HO%=&5CFFF ELSE HO%=&FFD71FC
>240 REPEAT
>250 WAIT:X%=(ZA0%-(F%>>2)) MOD 632:!J0%=X%+K0%:!J1%=X%+K1%:X%=(ZA1%-(F%>>1)) MOD 632:!J2%=X%+K2%:!J3%=X%+K3%
>252 X%=(ZA2%-F%) MOD 632:!J4%=X%+K4%:!J5%=X%+K5%:X%=(ZA3%-2*F%) MOD 632:!J6%=X%+K6%:!J7%=X%+K7%
>254 ?&D702=DL% DIV 65536:?&D704=0:?&D701=(DL% DIV 256) AND 255:?&D705=DL% AND 255:EI:IF SW% THEN PROCsoft
>260 IF G% THEN IF (F% AND 3)=0 THEN FOR I%=0 TO N%-1:V%(I%)=V%(I%)+65536:NEXT
>270 DI:?HO%=1:TA%=TB%:FOR I%=0 TO N%-1:P%=P%(I%)+V%(I%)
>280 IF (P% AND &FFFF)>632 OR P%>>>16>392 THEN PROCwall
>300 P%(I%)=P%:!TA%=P% AND &3FF03FF:TA%=TA%+32:NEXT
>320 ?HO%=0:IF K%=0 THEN PROCspr
>330 F%=F%+1:UNTIL F%=BN%
>340 T%=TIME-T%:IF RS% THEN PROCtext:PRINT BN%;" frames in ";T%;" cs, ";NP%;" pairs"
>350 END
>1000 REM ---- pairs ----
>1002 REM PROChit (ON COLLISION; B65 acknowledged the engine): CN% = number of
>1004 REM collided objects, table byte CA% = objects CI%-8..CI%-1 (a bit each),
>1006 REM zero bytes skipped, stop when CN% objects were seen; PROCbits: one
>1008 REM COLLIDE per set bit (LB%?m = its lowest set bit). No REM or WHILE in
>1009 REM the lines that run per frame (REM is skipped character by character).
>1010 DEF PROChit
>1020 CN%=?&FFD7286+256*?&FFD7287:CA%=&FFD7200:CI%=0
>1030 REPEAT CM%=?CA%:CA%=CA%+1:CI%=CI%+8:IF CM% THEN PROCbits
>1040 UNTIL CN%<=0 OR CI%>=N%:ENDPROC
>1045 DEF PROCbits
>1050 REPEAT CH%=CI%-8+LB%?CM%:CM%=CM% AND CM%-1:CN%=CN%-1:CQ%=COLLIDE(CH%):IF CQ%>CH% THEN A%=CH%:B%=CQ%:PROCpair
>1055 UNTIL CM%=0:ENDPROC
>1057 REM PROCpair: A%, B%: confirm (centre distance), swap, one step each
>1058 REM (if inside). D% = dX+8 + 65536*(dY+8); DT%?(dX+8+32*(dY+8)) = 1 for
>1059 REM dX*dX+dY*dY <= 64
>1060 DEF PROCpair
>1070 D%=P%(B%)-P%(A%)+&80008:IF D% AND &FFE0FFE0 THEN ENDPROC
>1075 IF DT%?((D% AND 31)+(D%>>>11))=0 THEN ENDPROC
>1080 NP%=NP%+1:U%=V%(A%):V%(A%)=V%(B%):V%(B%)=U%
>1090 U%=P%(A%)+V%(A%):IF (U% AND &FFFF)<=632 AND U%>>>16<=392 THEN P%(A%)=U%
>1100 U%=P%(B%)+V%(B%):IF (U% AND &FFFF)<=632 AND U%>>>16<=392 THEN P%(B%)=U%
>1110 ENDPROC
>1135 DEF PROCwall:LOCAL X%,Y%,U%,W%:REM reflect the velocity at a wall
>1136 X%=P%(I%) AND &FFFF:Y%=P%(I%)>>>16:U%=(V%(I%) AND &FFFF EOR &8000)-&8000:W%=(V%(I%)-U%) DIV 65536
>1137 IF X%+U%<0 OR X%+U%>632 THEN U%=-U%
>1138 IF Y%+W%<0 OR Y%+W%>392 THEN W%=-W%
>1139 V%(I%)=U%+W%*65536:P%=P%(I%)+V%(I%):ENDPROC
>1140 DEF PROCsoft:LOCAL I%,J%:REM without the engine: all pairs in BASIC (box test)
>1150 FOR I%=0 TO N%-2:FOR J%=I%+1 TO N%-1
>1160 IF ABS((P%(J%) AND &FFFF)-(P%(I%) AND &FFFF))<8 AND ABS((P%(J%)>>>16)-(P%(I%)>>>16))<8 THEN A%=I%:B%=J%:PROCpair
>1170 NEXT:NEXT:ENDPROC
>1180 DEF PROCtables:LOCAL I%,J%,X%:REM LB%?m: lowest set bit of m; DT%: see 1058
>1185 FOR I%=1 TO 255:J%=0:WHILE (I% AND 1<<J%)=0:J%=J%+1:ENDWHILE:LB%?I%=J%:NEXT
>1190 FOR I%=0 TO 543:X%=(I% AND 31)-8:J%=I% DIV 32-8:DT%?I%=-(X%*X%+J%*J%<=64):NEXT:ENDPROC
>1200 REM ---- set-up ----
>1210 DEF PROCballs:LOCAL C%,R%,M%,X%,Y%,D%,V%
>1220 REM six shaded balls (8x8 full colour, lit from the top left) at GA% =
>1230 REM glyphs &1800-&1805: palette ramps (first entry, length)
>1240 RESTORE 1300:FOR C%=0 TO 5:READ R%,M%:FOR Y%=0 TO 7:FOR X%=0 TO 7:V%=0
>1250 IF (2*X%-7)*(2*X%-7)+(2*Y%-7)*(2*Y%-7)<=60 THEN D%=(2*X%-4)*(2*X%-4)+(2*Y%-4)*(2*Y%-4):V%=R%+M%-1-D%*(M%-1) DIV 110:IF V%<R% THEN V%=R%
>1260 ?(GA%+64*C%+8*Y%+X%)=V%:NEXT:NEXT:NEXT:ENDPROC
>1300 DATA 97,11, 184,16, 152,16, 128,16, 168,16, 64,16
>1400 DEF PROCscreen:LOCAL I%,R%,A%,X%,C%
>1410 REM K325T: token lists (one per ball colour) and their colour words;
>1420 REM object table: X/Y, mask, height, bits 19-16, collision group 1, list,
>1430 REM colour offset, stride, box width BW%
>1440 IF K% THEN FOR C%=0 TO 5:PROCw(OA%+16*C%,&1800+C%):PROCw(OA%+16*C%+2,&FFFF):PROCw(CR%-&4000+OC%+16*C%,0):NEXT
>1450 IF K% THEN FOR I%=0 TO N%-1:A%=TB%+32*I%:C%=I% MOD 6:!A%=P%(I%):?(A%+4)=255:?(A%+5)=1:?(A%+6)=8:?(A%+7)=1:!(A%+8)=&9000+16*C%+(OC%+16*C%)*65536:!(A%+12)=BW%*65536:NEXT
>1455 REM XCTL bit 3 (newer K325T bitstreams): unpainted pixels show the background,
>1456 REM so sparse rows need no opaque base (ZB%=0); unimplemented bits read 0
>1458 ZB%=TRUE:IF K% THEN ?&FFD71F0=?&FFD71F0 OR 8:ZB%=(?&FFD71F0 AND 8)=0
>1460 PROCplanes
>1500 REM VIC-IV (HOTREG off): V400, 50 rows, one line per glyph row, CHR16 +
>1510 REM full colour above 255, rows of L%/2 tokens, pointers; list mode v2 with
>1515 REM the fast token path (XCTL bit 7)
>1520 ?&D05D=?&D05D AND 127:?&D031=?&D031 OR 8:?&D07B=49:?&D05B=0:?&D054=?&D054 OR 5
>1530 PROCw(&D058,L%):?&D05E=L% DIV 2:?&D063=?&D063 AND 192:?&D020=0:?&D021=0
>1540 ?&D060=0:?&D061=(S% DIV 256) AND 255:?&D062=S% DIV 65536:PROCw(&D064,&4000)
>1550 IF K% THEN ?&FFD71F8=0:?&FFD71F9=&C0:?&FFD71FA=8:?&FFD71FB=N%:?&FFD71F0=?&FFD71F0 OR &D0:PROCxctl2(1)
>1560 ENDPROC
>1600 DEF PROCsprites:LOCAL I%,Y%,X%
>1610 REM no list mode: balls 0-7 as sprites (8x8 circle, scaled to 320x200)
>1620 FOR Y%=0 TO 20:FOR X%=0 TO 2:?(&5FC00+3*Y%+X%)=0:NEXT:NEXT
>1630 RESTORE 1650:FOR Y%=0 TO 7:READ X%:?(&5FC00+3*Y%)=X%:NEXT
>1640 ?&D06C=0:?&D06D=&FA:?&D06E=&85:FOR I%=0 TO 7:PROCw(&5FA00+2*I%,&17F0):?(&D027+I%)=2+I%:NEXT:?&D015=255:ENDPROC
>1650 DATA 60,126,255,255,255,255,126,60
>1660 DEF PROCspr:LOCAL I%,X%:?&D010=0
>1670 FOR I%=0 TO 7:X%=24+(P%(I%) AND &FFFF) DIV 2:?(&D000+2*I%)=X% AND 255:IF X%>255 THEN ?&D010=?&D010 OR 1<<I%
>1680 ?(&D001+2*I%)=50+(P%(I%)>>>16) DIV 2:NEXT:ENDPROC
>1700 DEF PROCtext:?&D015=0:IF K% THEN ON COLLISION OFF:PROCxctl2(0):?&FFD71F0=?&FFD71F0 AND &27
>1710 ?&D031=V1%:?&D05B=V5%:?&D07B=V7%:PROCpalrest:MODE 0:ENDPROC
>1720 DEF PROCw(A%,V%):?A%=V% AND 255:?(A%+1)=(V% DIV 256) AND 255:ENDPROC
>1800 REM ---- background: four parallax star planes (sparse RRB) ----
>1802 REM Each row (L% bytes): SG% groups of 4 x (GOTOX, star glyph
>1803 REM GA%/64+6+plane), plane 0 (far, dim dot) .. 3 (near, bright). Without
>1804 REM XCTL bit 3 (ZB%) the VIC-IV keeps old pixels in its raster buffer where
>1805 REM a row paints nothing: then each row starts with GOTOX 0 (opaque) + 80
>1806 REM black glyphs. The star part of a row is 16*SG% bytes; there (in the
>1807 REM rows, or with the base in a staging area ZS%) the GOTOX words of one
>1808 REM plane are every 16 bytes, so per frame one DMA job per plane and byte
>1809 REM (X lo, X hi) rewrites all of them (with the base, 50 row jobs then copy
>1810 REM the star parts into the rows). The plane jobs copy with source step ZD(p)
>1812 REM from ramp tables ZL%/ZH% (lo/hi byte of n MOD 632, n < 80896; K325T:
>1814 REM chip RAM banks 9-11, else attic RAM): star k of plane p is at X =
>1816 REM (ZA(p) - offset + k*ZD(p)) MOD 632 (X <= 631: the glyph ends inside the
>1817 REM row; a star leaving at the left comes back at the right). Offsets F%/4,
>1818 REM F%/2, F%, 2*F%. Star GOTOX colour flags &90: transparent.
>1820 DEF PROCplanes:LOCAL I%,Q%,J%,D%,A%
>1821 SO%=-162*ZB%:L%=SO%+16*SG%:ZW%=S%:IF ZB% THEN ZW%=ZS%
>1822 ZN%=50*SG%:DL%=&5C000:ZT%=&5CA00
>1824 FOR I%=0 TO 631:?(ZL%+I%)=I% AND 255:?(ZH%+I%)=I% DIV 256:NEXT
>1826 I%=632:REPEAT PROCdma(0,I%,ZL%,ZL%+I%,1,1):PROCdma(0,I%,ZH%,ZH%+I%,1,1):I%=I%*2:UNTIL I%>72000
>1827 PROCdma(3,50*L%,0,S%,1,1):PROCdma(3,50*L%,0,CR%,1,1)
>1828 I%=GA% DIV 64+10:IF ZB% THEN PROCdma(3,80,I% AND 255,S%+2,1,2):PROCdma(3,80,I% DIV 256,S%+3,1,2)
>1829 IF ZB% THEN FOR I%=1 TO 49:PROCdma(0,162,S%,S%+I%*L%,1,1):NEXT
>1830 FOR I%=0 TO 49:IF ZB% THEN ?(CR%+I%*L%)=&10
>1831 PROCdma(3,4*SG%,&90,CR%+I%*L%+SO%,1,4):NEXT
>1832 FOR Q%=0 TO 3:I%=GA% DIV 64+6+Q%:PROCdma(3,ZN%,I% AND 255,ZW%+4*Q%+2,1,16):PROCdma(3,ZN%,I% DIV 256,ZW%+4*Q%+3,1,16):NEXT
>1834 RESTORE 1850:FOR I%=0 TO 319:?(GA%+64*6+I%)=0:NEXT:FOR Q%=0 TO 3:READ ZD%(Q%),ZA%(Q%),J%
>1836 FOR I%=1 TO J%:READ A%,D%:?(GA%+64*(6+Q%)+A%)=D%:NEXT:NEXT
>1838 FOR J%=0 TO 7:Q%=J% DIV 2:A%=DL%+22*J%:?A%=&80:?(A%+1)=ZL% DIV &100000:?(A%+2)=&81:?(A%+3)=0:?(A%+4)=&83:?(A%+5)=ZD%(Q%):?(A%+6)=&85:?(A%+7)=16
>1840 D%=ZW%+4*Q%+(J% AND 1):I%=ZL%:IF J% AND 1 THEN I%=ZH%
>1841 PROCjob(A%+8,4*((J%<7) OR ZB%)*-1,ZN%,I%,D%):ZK%(J%)=(I% AND &FFFFF)+(D% AND 255)*&1000000:NEXT
>1843 IF ZB% THEN FOR J%=0 TO 49:A%=DL%+176+22*J%:?A%=&80:?(A%+1)=0:?(A%+2)=&81:?(A%+3)=0:?(A%+4)=&83:?(A%+5)=1:?(A%+6)=&85:?(A%+7)=1:PROCjob(A%+8,4*(J%<49)*-1,16*SG%,ZS%+16*SG%*J%,S%+L%*J%+162):NEXT
>1845 J0%=DL%+13:J1%=J0%+22:J2%=J1%+22:J3%=J2%+22:J4%=J3%+22:J5%=J4%+22:J6%=J5%+22:J7%=J6%+22
>1846 K0%=ZK%(0):K1%=ZK%(1):K2%=ZK%(2):K3%=ZK%(3):K4%=ZK%(4):K5%=ZK%(5):K6%=ZK%(6):K7%=ZK%(7)
>1847 ZA0%=ZA%(0)+632*&200000:ZA1%=ZA%(1)+632*&200000:ZA2%=ZA%(2)+632*&200000:ZA3%=ZA%(3)+632*&200000:ENDPROC
>1848 REM per plane: source step, start, pixels (offset in the glyph, colour)
>1850 DATA 251,0,1, 27,170
>1852 DATA 145,301,1, 27,175
>1854 DATA 171,612,4, 27,179,28,179,35,179,36,179
>1856 DATA 147,845,10, 19,178,20,178,26,178,27,183,28,183,29,178,34,178,35,183,36,183,37,178
>1860 DEF PROCjob(J%,C%,N%,S%,D%)
>1862 ?J%=&0B:?(J%+1)=0:?(J%+2)=C%:?(J%+3)=N% AND 255:?(J%+4)=N% DIV 256
>1864 !(J%+5)=S% AND &FFFFF:!(J%+8)=D% AND &FFFFF:?(J%+12)=0:?(J%+13)=0:ENDPROC
>1866 DEF PROCdma(C%,N%,S%,D%,SS%,DS%):?ZT%=&80:?(ZT%+1)=S% DIV &100000:?(ZT%+2)=&81:?(ZT%+3)=D% DIV &100000
>1868 ?(ZT%+4)=&83:?(ZT%+5)=SS%:?(ZT%+6)=&85:?(ZT%+7)=DS%:PROCjob(ZT%+8,C%,N%,S%,D%)
>1870 ?&D702=ZT% DIV 65536:?&D704=0:?&D701=(ZT% DIV 256) AND 255:?&D705=ZT% AND 255:ENDPROC
>2000 DEF PROCpalette:LOCAL S%,C%,D%,I%,R0%,G0%,B0%,R1%,G1%,B1%
>2010 REM own palette: ramps from 16 on (0-15 stay the standard colours)
>2020 RESTORE 2060
>2030 READ S%:IF S%<0 THEN ENDPROC
>2040 READ C%,R0%,G0%,B0%,R1%,G1%,B1%:D%=C%-1:IF D%<1 THEN D%=1
>2045 FOR I%=0 TO C%-1
>2050 PROCpal(S%+I%,R0%+(R1%-R0%)*I% DIV D%,G0%+(G1%-G0%)*I% DIV D%,B0%+(B1%-B0%)*I% DIV D%):NEXT:GOTO 2030
>2060 DATA 16,32,14,18,70,255,190,140, 48,16,40,22,10,190,140,80, 64,16,30,35,60,175,185,215
>2070 DATA 80,16,5,35,10,110,200,70, 97,11,90,0,0,255,140,120, 108,2,60,40,20,120,90,50
>2080 DATA 110,2,110,60,20,170,110,50, 113,8,50,55,70,235,240,250, 121,4,200,150,0,255,230,90
>2090 DATA 125,1,90,170,255,90,170,255, 126,2,30,30,40,220,30,30, 128,16,90,30,0,255,240,150
>2100 DATA 144,8,0,0,0,40,35,55, 152,16,20,60,15,200,235,110, 168,16,130,150,190,255,255,255
>2110 DATA 184,16,20,25,70,140,170,240, 200,16,45,25,10,190,130,70, 216,40,0,0,0,255,255,255, -1
>2120 DEF PROCpal(I%,R%,G%,B%):REM the VIC-IV stores palette bytes nibble-swapped
>2130 ?(&D100+I%)=(R% MOD 16)*16+R% DIV 16:?(&D200+I%)=(G% MOD 16)*16+G% DIV 16:?(&D300+I%)=(B% MOD 16)*16+B% DIV 16:ENDPROC
>2140 DEF PROCpalsave:LOCAL I%
>2150 FOR I%=16 TO 255:?(&5F400+I%)=?(&D100+I%):?(&5F500+I%)=?(&D200+I%):?(&5F600+I%)=?(&D300+I%):NEXT:ENDPROC
>2160 DEF PROCpalrest:LOCAL I%
>2170 FOR I%=16 TO 255:?(&D100+I%)=?(&5F400+I%):?(&D200+I%)=?(&5F500+I%):?(&D300+I%)=?(&5F600+I%):NEXT:ENDPROC
>9000 DEF PROCxctl2(B%):REM XCTL2 bit 0 (4-pixel painting, with XCTL bits 4 and 7) from feature level 4
>9010 IF ?&FFD71FD>=4 THEN ?&FFD71F1=(?&FFD71F1 AND &FE) OR B%
>9020 ENDPROC
>120 BN%=150:RS%=0:N%=8:G%=0:SW%=1:BW%=6
>350 PROCtext:S%=0:FOR I%=0 TO N%-1:S%=S%+(P%(I%) AND &FFFF)*3+(P%(I%)>>>16)*7+V%(I%) MOD 9973:NEXT:PRINT "pairs ";NP%;" sum ";S%:END
>RUN
Bounce: 8 balls
pairs 8 sum 860
>
